# Minimal synthetic material-library stub (map_Kd lines added 2026-10-02: a material without one bakes as the
# missing texture - every golem drew magenta/black; "#name" binds the model JSON's own "textures" entry of that name), added 2026-09-25 - NOT recovered original data (the true original
# never shipped a .mtl for these models either; its own bespoke 1.12.2-era OBJ loader never needed material-
# driven texture resolution). NeoForge's own modern ObjLoader eagerly resolves any `mtllib` directive it finds
# and throws if the referenced file is missing, so this exists purely to satisfy that real parse-time
# requirement - the actual texture is supplied per-part by the model JSON's own "textures" map, not read from
# here. Shared by golem_base.obj and golem_base_flag.obj (both reference this exact file name).
newmtl Material__25
	map_Kd #Material__25
